WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.009
(dramatic music begins)

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:07.572
- [Newsman] The president's
car is now turning

00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:11.143
on to Elm Street in open limousine parade.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.280
(gunshot fires)

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.860
- [Johnny] There's a cover-up
that's about to happen here.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.237
- [Newsman] This is a
situation and I read,

00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:20.060
"Kennedy is shot in head."

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.070
- [Johnny] The
assassination of a president

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.140
and then a scramble by the U.S. government

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.420
to hide information from its people.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.192
- So much information was
hid from the American public.

00:00:30.192 --> 00:00:32.662
- [Lyndon] How many, how many,
how many shots were fired?

00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:34.910
- [J. Edgar] Three.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.850
- [Johnny] The question
of who shot JFK and why

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.680
has riveted America since that
horrifying day 60 years ago.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.640
But over time, it's become
clear that the FBI and CIA

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.710
kept information hidden,

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.170
not just from the public,
but from the commission

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.780
in charge of investigating
the assassination.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.060
This has fueled an understandable doubt

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.560
in the official account,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.900
including, by the way, Lyndon B. Johnson,

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.300
the president who took JFK's place.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.580
Congress even came out
in the '80s saying that

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.400
this was probably a conspiracy,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.170
and the public ran wild with this.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.210
They came up with hundreds of suspects

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.420
of who could have been
involved in the assassination.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.870
Theories like this thrive
when government authorities

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.883
aren't transparent with their people.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.500
So let me show you how this happened.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.360
Let me explain the official story

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.970
and why that story has been
hit with a wave of doubt

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.140
over the decades

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.320
and explain that unlike a
lot of conspiracy theories,

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.810
doubting the official story here

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.914
isn't as crazy as you might think.

00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:41.164
(tense dramatic music)

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.750
- [Journalist] This was a turning
point in American history.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.547
People all of a sudden decided,

00:01:53.547 --> 00:01:55.747
"I'm not sure they're
telling us the truth."

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:03.110
- JFK is this really
symbolic character who lived

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.690
during a very, very important
time in American history,

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:08.810
and the story really
dives into the context

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.450
of what it was like to be
in America in the '60s.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.910
I'm really excited to dive in
and show you all of the stuff.

