00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.120
Let's dive back in to
this fascinating story

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.082
of what happened to JFK.

00:03:34.082 --> 00:03:38.270
(typewriter keyboard clacking)
(tense suspenseful music)

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.430
People loved John Kennedy.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.290
He was this good-looking guy

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.660
who was always hanging out
with his beautiful family

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.910
and he just seemed to
instill a sense of confidence

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:47.743
in people.

00:03:47.743 --> 00:03:50.030
Kennedy rode this positive
perception up the ranks

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:52.940
of American politics to
become the 35th president.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.350
This was in the early '60s

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.110
when America was in a
giant time of transition.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.790
- Oh, this is a revolution, of course,

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.590
that is sweeping our country now.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.750
- The U.S. was the global superpower

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.480
and was locked in a Cold
War with another empire

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.680
a world away.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.600
So JFK walks into the presidency

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.560
to find his military
and intelligence leaders

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.420
causing a lot of trouble around the world.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.750
They had become very comfortable
with dangerous secrets.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.310
They were funding wars,

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.130
they were overthrowing
governments in faraway countries,

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.900
they were assassinating leaders

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.670
that threatened American interests,

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.830
and they were doing most
of this totally in secret.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.663
By the way,

00:04:28.663 --> 00:04:30.350
if you wanna know more
about those CIA shenanigans,

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.750
go watch the video where
we map all the U.S. coups.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.870
Anyway, JFK walks in and
sees this as "too much."

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.630
He wants to reign in these
spy and military leaders

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.330
from what he sees as an
abuse of American power.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.030
He ended up firing and demoting
a bunch of these leaders,

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.160
a lot of these intel and military guys

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.650
who were plotting and
executing covert operations

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:49.483
around the world,

00:04:49.483 --> 00:04:52.700
and he continued to pursue
like his ideal of world peace.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.500
He chose diplomacy over violence.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.290
When nuclear-armed missiles
were found in Cuba,

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.520
he slowed down the momentum

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.010
towards a full-scale presence in Vietnam

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.920
and he shut down several
of these covert operations

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.350
that were being planned
by the leaders around him.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.200
This caused great tension between JFK

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.600
and America's military and spy leadership.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.280
All of this context is important

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.153
when we look back on that
day in November 1963.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.420
- [Newsman] Friday morning, 11:37,

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.812
the President's jet lands
at the Dallas Airport.

00:05:22.812 --> 00:05:27.812
(typewriter keyboard clacking)
(tense suspenseful music)

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:31.790
- [Johnny] President Kennedy

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.560
and the Vice President Lyndon B. Johnson

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.420
arrived to Dallas for a speech

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.740
that the President was to give.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.370
He got in this open-top
limousine with his wife, Jackie,

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.620
and the Texas governor, John Connally,

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.063
along with his wife, Nellie.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.290
They rode through these streets,

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.173
downtown Dallas lined
with cheering spectators,

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.082
and then gunshots rang out.

00:05:56.082 --> 00:05:57.530
(gunshot fires)

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.270
- [Newsman] Kennedy
apparently shot in head.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:01.010
Blood was on his head.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.650
- [Johnny] The shots hit the
President in the neck and head,

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.483
also wounding Governor Connally.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.610
The President was rushed to the hospital

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.323
where he was pronounced dead.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:19.643
- And very often, you'll find
a zipper hidden in the arm.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.560
- Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.180
You'll excuse the fact
that I'm out of breath,

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.250
but President Kennedy and
Governor John Connally

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.580
have been cut down by assassins'
bullets in downtown Dallas.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.921
The President has rushed
to Parkland Hospital.

00:06:33.921 --> 00:06:37.421
(tense suspenseful music)

00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:42.560
(tense suspenseful music)
(typewriter keyboard clacking)

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.270
- [Johnny] Within hours
of the assassination,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.810
the prime suspect became this
24-year-old former Marine,

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.160
a self-declared communist

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.080
who had renounced his American citizenship

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.150
and moved to the Soviet Union,

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:56.060
where he then fell disenchanted
with life in Russia

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.440
and move back to the U.S.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.450
Eventually, ending up on the sixth story

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.640
of this building in Dallas where he worked

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:04.250
and where he was on
that morning in November

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.190
where he aimed a rifle
and shot the President.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.040
His name was Lee Harvey Oswald.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.200
And after these shots rang out, he fled.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.440
While on the run, he shot and
killed a Dallas police officer

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.390
before hiding in a movie theater

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:18.890
and then eventually being arrested

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.020
at around 2:15 PM that day.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:23.030
- I didn't shoot anybody, no, Sir.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.380
- There was to be a trial,

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.020
and Oswald planned to plead not guilty,

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.030
claiming the whole thing
was actually a setup.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:30.023
- I'm just a patsy.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.350
- Patsy, which is like an old-timey term

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:36.020
for like the fall guy,
the one who was setup.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:38.780
That same day, the vice
president, Lyndon B. Johnson,

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:41.180
was rushed back to the presidential plane

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.600
and sworn in as the new
president of the United States

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.850
before taking off and
heading back to Washington.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.830
At the same time, the FBI,

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.680
the top investigatory body in our country,

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.270
descends onto Dallas.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.750
And very quickly, the director
of the FBI, J. Edgar Hoover,

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.220
who's a big part of the story,

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.800
he comes to a conclusion
as to what happened.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.320
This is before any investigation
had really gone forth.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.480
And Hoover decides that Oswald

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:07.190
absolutely was the one who did it.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.960
He was a communist sympathizer,

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.520
he was a frustrated misfit,

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.770
and crucially, he acted alone.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:13.640
There was no one else.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.440
Here's a phone call between Hoover

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.270
and the new president, LBJ.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:20.030
- [J. Edgar] There's no question
but that he is the man now.

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:22.348
The fingerprints and things we have.

00:08:22.348 --> 00:08:24.277
- I'd like some legal representation,

00:08:24.277 --> 00:08:27.623
but you, police officers, have
not allowed me to have any.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.800
- But luckily, we have a justice system

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.660
and we would find what
the facts actually say.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.400
Oswald was going to stand trial

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.320
where the evidence could
be thoroughly examined,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.330
where the country could see for themselves

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.460
who actually shot their President

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.710
and get closure on this horrifying event,

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.863
where whoever did it could
actually be brought to justice.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.993
But that never happened.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.960
Two days after the assassination,

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.760
while Oswald was being transferred

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.040
from police headquarters
to the county jail,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.230
a nightclub owner named Jack Ruby

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.750
jumped out in front of the
crowd of police officers

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.649
and news reporters and shot Oswald.

00:09:01.649 --> 00:09:03.980
(gunshot fires)

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.780
He was quickly rushed to the hospital

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.370
where he died soon after,

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.070
the same hospital where
President Kennedy had died

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.900
just 48 hours earlier.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.340
- Lee Oswald has been shot.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:14.998
- I think he got what he deserved,

00:09:14.998 --> 00:09:16.127
if he's the one that did it.

00:09:16.127 --> 00:09:18.800
- It is difficult to say
how long it will take

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.520
for the full realization of
what happened to really sink in.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.250
- With Oswald dead,
there could be no trial,

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.020
no real sense of justice.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:30.170
This left the government
investigators, the FBI mostly,

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.140
with the opportunity to
really own the narrative

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.100
of what happened.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.000
The very next day,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.240
the Deputy Attorney General
sends a memo to the White House

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.150
stressing that the
public must be satisfied

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:44.750
with this explanation
that Oswald acted alone.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.120
He didn't have co-conspirators
that were still at large.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.330
This had to be the story, and
I'll explain why in a sec.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.940
This memo also included some wisdom

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.130
and kind of a foreshadow
of what was gonna happen

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.810
over the next several decades

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.540
where the memo urges the
White House to release

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.120
as much information as
possible to the public

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.670
so as to avoid public speculation.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.297
Just remember that advice,

00:10:06.297 --> 00:10:09.620
"Release the information to
avoid public speculation."

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.270
It's kinda the most
important part of the story.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.060
We have these recently
released phone recordings

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.160
between the FBI director, J. Edgar Hoover,

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.720
and the new president, LBJ,

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.340
and we see in this phone call

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:23.554
that the FBI actually didn't
want a thorough investigation.

00:10:23.554 --> 00:10:25.690
- [Lyndon] I think it
would be very, very bad

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.890
to have a rash of investigations.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.540
- [J. Edgar] It'd be a three-ring circus.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.660
- [Lyndon] Well, the only
way to stop them is probably

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.210
to appoint a high level one
to evaluate your report.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:38.462
I can select out of the government,

00:10:38.462 --> 00:10:40.400
and I could tell the House and Senate

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.200
not to go ahead with the investigation.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.033
- [J. Edgar] Yes.

00:10:43.033 --> 00:10:46.460
- LBJ creates this group
called the Warren Commission,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.140
and you can see in these phone calls,

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.030
he was asking the FBI director

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.680
who should be on the Commission.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.566
- [Lyndon] What do you
think about Allen Dulles?

00:10:53.566 --> 00:10:55.910
- [J. Edgar] I think
he would be a good man.

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:57.200
- [Johnny] Wait, did you catch that?

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.400
Allen Dulles,

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.470
he was the former director of the CIA.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.330
He's one of the guys that JFK fired

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:04.400
after he tried to overthrow
the Cuban government.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.590
And now, he's about to be
appointed to the committee

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:09.350
investigating Kennedy's assassination.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.620
This did nothing to instill
trust in the Commission.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.300
- The new president appointed a Commission

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.040
of seven prominent Americans

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.780
to investigate the whole affair.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.573
- [Lyndon] The Special
Commission will have before it

00:11:19.573 --> 00:11:22.160
all the evidence uncovered
by the Federal Bureau

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.077
of Investigation and all the information

00:11:24.077 --> 00:11:26.870
available to any agencies
of the Federal Government.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.360
- The Warren Commission
was given just 10 months

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:32.300
to investigate this
situation using the evidence

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.970
that was mostly provided
to them by the FBI.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.560
They produced this report,

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:38.690
which essentially confirms the conclusion

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:41.870
that J. Edgar Hoover, the
director of the FBI, had come to

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.630
in the hours and days
following the assassination,

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.250
that on November 22nd,

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.380
the shots fired that killed the President

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:51.260
and wounded the Governor
were fired by one guy,

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:52.730
Lee Harvey Oswald.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.220
The report stresses that he acted alone.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.690
They say it very definitively.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.140
He nor the person who killed
him two days later, Jack Ruby,

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:03.650
were a part of any conspiracy,
domestic or foreign.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:05.870
All of the shots came solely

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.940
from the sixth floor of this building,

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:11.630
and crucially, there were
only three shots fired.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:12.626
Three bullets.

00:12:12.626 --> 00:12:15.110
- [Lyndon] How many, how many,
how many shots were fired?

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:15.943
- [J. Edgar] Three.

00:12:15.943 --> 00:12:17.150
- [Lyndon] Any of them fired at me?

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.082
- [J. Edgar] No.

00:12:18.082 --> 00:12:19.394
- [Lyndon] All three to the President?

00:12:19.394 --> 00:12:20.227
- [J. Edgar] All three to the President,

00:12:20.227 --> 00:12:21.060
and we have them.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:27.200
- [Johnny] The report
says that the first bullet

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.240
likely missed the car completely,

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.470
but that the second one did
something very interesting.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.050
It first hit the president in the back

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.510
and then exited his chest.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:40.880
It then entered through
the governor's back,

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.150
went through his rib, and
then exited through his chest,

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.170
but it wasn't done yet.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.890
It then entered his wrist,
shattering the wrist bone,

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:50.150
and then exited the wrist

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.540
and went partially into
the governor's leg.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.890
Whoa, okay.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.390
It's quite the journey for one bullet.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:57.920
Oh, and the bullet in question,

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.650
which just apparently made seven wounds,

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.780
supposedly looked like this,

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.700
which some ballistic experts have said

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.980
looks a little too pristine for a bullet

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.590
that allegedly just went
through two human bodies.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:10.850
And then, of course, the third bullet,

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.050
according to the Warren Commission,

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:13.280
was the one that delivered

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:15.500
the fatal headshot to the President.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.930
This was the explanation
that the Warren Commission

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.390
came up with to explain all of the wounds

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:21.830
that were found on the victims.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:25.190
All of this damage had to be
done with just three bullets,

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:26.960
and why just three bullets?

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:30.267
Again, ask J. Edgar Hoover
right after the assassination.

00:13:30.267 --> 00:13:31.970
- [J. Edgar] On that floor,

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.273
we found the three empty
shells that had been fired.

00:13:35.273 --> 00:13:39.080
- They only found three
shells up on that sixth floor.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.550
So if all of this damage was done

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:41.960
with more than three bullets,

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.990
that would mean that there had
to be more than one shooter.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.310
A conspiracy.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.690
But there couldn't be a conspiracy.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.060
Hoover had adopted this line of thinking

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.560
right after the assassination,

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.420
this assumption that it was just one guy,

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:55.130
and that line of thinking

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:57.410
endured into the Warren Commission,

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.210
a commission that Hoover himself

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.013
helped the President assemble.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.600
In the end, the Commission used

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:08.960
a lot of cherry-picked evidence
provided to them by the FBI

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.510
that supported their
already-drawn conclusions.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.730
And in the process, they turned any focus

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:16.130
away from exploring all
of the possibilities,

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.290
including the possibility of a conspiracy.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.220
The report focuses almost
entirely on one guy,

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.980
Lee Harvey Oswald, and his three bullets.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:27.380
- Who killed John F. Kennedy?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:31.190
The Commission answers
unequivocally, "Lee Harvey Oswald."

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:33.020
Was Oswald a member of a conspiracy?

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:35.810
The Commission answers, "He acted alone."

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.540
- They ignored witnesses that
contradicted their stories.

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.850
They ignored or modified
the signed reports

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.820
from surgeons and doctors who
worked with President Kennedy

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.950
immediately after he
arrived to the hospital

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:49.430
that said that the wounds in
the President's neck-chest area

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.470
looked like they came in from the front,

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.090
meaning not from this building

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:54.470
that was behind the President.

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:57.560
In other words, the FBI
and the Warren Commission

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.360
ignored the advice from that memo

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:03.890
that admonished the government
to release all of the facts.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:07.010
In my mind, this was the biggest mistake

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.320
and the root of all
the conspiracy theories

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:10.370
that exists today.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:13.400
The question I had in all of this is, why?

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.320
Why not do a proper investigation

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.780
that explores the possibility
that this was done

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:20.780
by a group of conspirators
instead of just one guy?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.430
For me, the answer to this question

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.950
has a lot to do with the greatest fears

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.800
that the American government
and people were facing

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.414
in the early 1960s.

00:15:29.414 --> 00:15:33.200
(tense suspenseful music)
(typewriter keyboard clacking)

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.740
First, we have to remember
that 1960s America

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.930
was right in the heart of the Cold War,

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:43.610
a time of constant vigilance
of fear of nuclear apocalypse,

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.610
of extreme tension between
these two superpowers.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.620
If this assassination was seen

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:51.140
as an attempt to topple the government.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:54.830
Or even worse, if it had been
organized by the Soviet Union

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.080
or its fellow communist regime in Cuba,

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.820
that would create a sense of panic

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:00.200
among the American public.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.060
It would be a very different situation

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.780
than a 24-year-old communist
sympathizer acting alone.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:08.420
A believed conspiracy
would also create pressure

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:11.000
from the American public to strike back,

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.560
which could lead to an escalation

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.840
with another nuclear-armed nation.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.730
Oh, and the CIA also had an incentive

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:20.090
to keep an investigation
from being too widespread.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:20.923
At the time,

00:16:20.923 --> 00:16:23.360
they were secretly conducting
all of these operations

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.210
to assassinate Cuba's
leader, Fidel Castro.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.330
This was a big deal and it
was a big secret at the time.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.840
Any deep investigation into
possible conspiracy with Cuba

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:35.360
might reveal that the CIA is trying

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:37.130
to assassinate Fidel Castro,

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.720
which would not be good for the CIA.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.280
So one way to read all of this,

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.620
the memos, the rushed conclusion,

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.780
the emphasis on Oswald acting alone,

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:46.790
the need for there to
only be three bullets,

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:49.010
you can see this as a bunch
of government officials

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:52.580
scrambling to keep the
American public calm

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.890
to make sure that
pandemonium doesn't break out

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:56.690
all while reducing the possibility

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.420
of geopolitical escalation
with the Soviet Union.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:01.490
You can see this in some
of these phone calls

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.740
where the new president is deeply worried

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.290
about keeping the American people united

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.660
around a simplified
narrative of what happened.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.420
He's worried that if
alternative theories get out,

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.090
it could threaten our entire system.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.880
So their tactic for doing this
was to hijack the narrative

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.580
to suppress and influence
the investigation

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:20.960
and make it very simple,

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.040
Oswald did it.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:22.873
That's it.

00:17:22.873 --> 00:17:23.706
Here's the problem though.

00:17:23.706 --> 00:17:26.180
Eventually, people will do the math

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:27.890
and realize that the government

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.740
has been keeping the
full picture from them,

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:32.744
and that's exactly what happens next.

00:17:32.744 --> 00:17:37.744
(tense suspenseful music)
(typewriter keyboard clacking)

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.680
So the Warren Commission files its report

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.690
with the official story of what happened,

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.880
but soon after they do so,

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.040
members of the Warren
Commission themselves

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.680
come out and say like they
don't actually believe the story

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.210
that the Warren Commission just put out,

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.580
especially when it comes
to the key assertion

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:58.910
that one bullet was responsible
for causing seven wounds.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.280
- I could not convince myself that

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:03.590
the same bullet struck both of them.

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:04.940
- [Interviewer] You
mean that you, yourself,

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.070
weren't convinced about
the single-bullet theory?

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:08.090
- No, I wasn't convinced.

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:08.990
- [Johnny] Governor Connally,

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.780
the one who was sitting in front of JFK

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:13.040
and the one who was supposedly shot

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.360
by that one single bullet,

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.740
he disagreed with the story.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.330
- I understand there's some question

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.640
in the minds of the experts
about whether or not

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.470
we could both have been
hit by the same bullet.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:23.270
I just don't happen to believe that.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:26.660
- Even the new president,
LBJ, wasn't totally convinced.

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.190
I mean, he was kind of secretive about it,

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:29.510
but he eventually did come out

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:30.920
and tell a reporter from the Atlantic

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.960
that he thought that
this was a conspiracy,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.570
that it was Cuba
retaliating against the U.S.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:38.840
for all of these CIA attempts
to assassinate their leader.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:43.190
This was not good for the Warren
Commission and their story.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:45.620
Then, 12 years after the assassination,

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.860
this full uncut version of a strip of film

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.980
that shows the assassination of JFK,

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.050
it finally airs on national TV.

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:57.380
- It's the film shot by the
Dallas dress manufacturer,

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:59.870
Abraham Zapruder,

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:02.633
and it's the execution
of President Kennedy.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.750
- This was the first time
that Americans could see

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.240
solid visual evidence of this event,

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.280
but why hadn't it been released earlier?

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.320
To some, this film contradicted

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.900
the official account from
the Warren Commission

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.660
and it sparked this new
demand for real answers

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:22.460
from a government that kept behaving

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:23.780
like it was hiding something.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:27.620
All of this is coinciding with
a time in American history

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.830
where Americans are losing
faith in the Federal Government.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.440
You just see this massive like nosedive.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.390
All of the CIA's covert operations

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:36.620
are starting to come to light,

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:40.160
the country is mired in
this endless war in Vietnam,

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.620
the President's people were
just found spying on their

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.780
political opponents in a hotel in D.C.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.780
Like, the government has not
earned our trust at this point,

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:48.777
so people are like,

00:19:48.777 --> 00:19:51.170
"It wouldn't be a far
stretch that the government

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.900
was also behind the assassination of JFK."

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:56.960
This was furthered by the
suspicious assassination

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.640
of Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.380
- Dr. Martin Luther King,

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.500
the apostle of non-violence
in the Civil Rights Movement

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.110
has been shot to death
in Memphis, Tennessee.

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:09.110
- This was all too much and
the people wanted answers.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.930
So in a shining moment of
redemption of our democracy,

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:14.480
Congress responded by forming a committee

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.090
that reopened the
investigations into these

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.280
two assassinations, JFK and MLK.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.020
This committee did a real investigation.

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:22.790
They actually were earnest about this

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.380
and they confirmed what a lot of Americans

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:25.550
were already feeling,

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.800
which is that the Warren
Commission's investigation

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.030
didn't sufficiently look

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.830
into the possibilities of a conspiracy.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.820
They say it point blank.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.160
They were way too fixated
on their assumptions

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.620
that it had to be this
lone gunman that did it

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.350
and that their conclusions
were way too definitive,

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:42.770
and then they specifically
call out the FBI and the CIA

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:45.380
for withholding information
from the investigation.

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:48.800
One FBI agent even testified
that he was ordered

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.020
by his superiors to destroy evidence.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.500
In this case, a letter that
Oswald had written to the FBI.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.990
- And he handed it to me and
he said, "Oswald's dead now.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:58.580
There can be no trial.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.140
Here, get rid of this."

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:04.130
- Why was the FBI asking its
agents to destroy evidence?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:07.940
The committee concluded that
it was a "high probability

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:11.090
that it was two gunmen that fired at JFK

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:13.400
and that it was probably a conspiracy."

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.240
That's what it says.

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:16.370
But they stopped short
of trying to determine

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.840
who that other gunman was

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.580
or who had organized the conspiracy.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.740
And then they once again
make the recommendation

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:24.590
that all of the information
on this topic be made public.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.840
- Isn't it time for the American people

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:30.350
to, at least, know what
happened at 12:30 PM

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:35.300
in Dallas, Texas on November 22nd, 1963?

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.370
- Quick caveat, the committee's conclusion

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.280
that the assassination
was probably a conspiracy

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.410
relied heavily on one piece of evidence,

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.930
which was the sound
recording from that day

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:47.450
where you can hear gunshots
and you hear more than three,

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.320
and it kind of inferred

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.180
that there were like multiple shooters.

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:52.070
This evidence was later challenged

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:54.110
and kind of debunked by the FBI,

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:57.327
but also a different research
facility that basically said,

00:21:57.327 --> 00:22:00.320
"This sound recording
wasn't even gunshots.

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:01.910
It wasn't even recorded during the time

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:02.870
of the assassination."

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:05.900
But to me, the whole conspiracy
thing was not actually

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:08.570
the most important part of
this committee's report.

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:11.030
The most important part
was that they confirmed

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:14.390
that the Warren Commission had
been cherry-picking evidence

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.310
and hiding stuff from the American people.

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:17.810
After the Congressional Committee

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:20.150
confirmed to the American
people that the FBI

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:22.190
and the CIA had been hiding evidence,

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:25.070
the conspiracy theories rose up once again

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:27.830
culminating in this
movie in the early '90s

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:30.350
that paints an alternative picture

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:31.880
of what could have happened here,

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:35.330
a shadowy government conspiracy
to kill the President,

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:39.620
or at least a conspiracy
to cover up the real story.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.040
- Oswald, Ruby, Cuba, the mafia,

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:44.990
keeps them guessing like
some kind of parlor game,

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:48.410
prevents them from asking the
most important question, why?

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:50.210
Why was Kennedy killed?

00:22:50.210 --> 00:22:51.053
Who benefited?

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:53.900
Who has the power to cover it up?

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:56.000
- The film was largely conjecture,

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.310
kind of based on some elements of truth,

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:01.160
and some might argue that it
was irresponsibly misleading

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:02.817
to, like, show the American public like,

00:23:02.817 --> 00:23:04.250
"Hey, the government
killed the President."

00:23:04.250 --> 00:23:06.770
But hey, in a world where the
government isn't being clear

00:23:06.770 --> 00:23:08.810
and forthright to the American people,

00:23:08.810 --> 00:23:11.690
this film felt like a response.

00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:13.820
Maybe the government was hiding the truth,

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:15.320
maybe the government did do it,

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:17.750
or maybe they're just
covering something up.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:19.790
We don't know because they
haven't released information.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:21.200
This was a popular movie

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:24.200
and people latched onto the
theories presented in this film.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.780
- The notion that there were
more than one set of shooters

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:29.540
the way that it's presented
physically in this movie

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:30.650
is highly convincing.

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:32.420
- Public pressure got so intense

00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:35.060
that Congress finally decided to do

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.680
what they should have done in the '60s,

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:39.320
which is force all of these agencies

00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:41.660
to release all of the information.

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:44.330
So in 1992, Congress passes this law

00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:46.910
that would lay the
foundation for releasing

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:49.700
all of the documents
related to the assassination

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:51.200
by October 2017.

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:52.100
That was the deadline.

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:54.440
They assembled a committee
and gave them several years

00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:55.940
to go through all of the documents

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:58.190
and reexamine the official account

00:23:58.190 --> 00:24:01.220
and prepare these documents
for release to the public.

00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:03.513
We actually talked to the
chairman of that committee.

00:24:03.513 --> 00:24:05.570
- I was nominated by President Clinton

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:09.440
to chair the Assassination
Records Review Board.

00:24:09.440 --> 00:24:12.170
- In the process of going over
all of this documentation,

00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:15.320
this review board found
some more inconsistencies

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:18.920
and discrepancies and instances
of potential cover-up,

00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:19.880
like the autopsy.

00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:22.160
There's an entire video I could
make about just the autopsy

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.900
and the missing brain and all of this,

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:27.590
but the crux of it is that what
the doctors and surgeons saw

00:24:27.590 --> 00:24:29.750
moments after the President was shot.

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:32.030
They recorded and they, like, wrote down,

00:24:32.030 --> 00:24:34.670
but then what the official autopsy record

00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:36.860
actually looked like when it was released

00:24:36.860 --> 00:24:38.810
was something very different.

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:40.340
The way the wounds were described,

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:41.570
where the wounds were,

00:24:41.570 --> 00:24:42.890
what the brain looked like,

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:46.670
all of this stuff had
been changed or modified.

00:24:46.670 --> 00:24:50.480
The photos themselves had
potentially been changed,

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.300
and then the brain itself
like literally went missing.

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:55.340
It's like unaccounted for.

00:24:55.340 --> 00:24:57.290
So anyway, that's an entire rabbit hole

00:24:57.290 --> 00:24:58.910
that you can go down if you want to.

00:24:58.910 --> 00:25:00.710
Releasing all these records also revealed

00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:03.470
that the CIA and FBI had been keeping tabs

00:25:03.470 --> 00:25:06.110
on Oswald's whereabouts,
which maybe makes sense

00:25:06.110 --> 00:25:07.850
because he was like a Soviet sympathizer,

00:25:07.850 --> 00:25:09.710
but like, why didn't we know that before?

00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:13.340
We learned that the Secret
Service had destroyed documents,

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:15.890
the original motorcade
route sheets that they had,

00:25:15.890 --> 00:25:17.780
the surveillance tapes from that day.

00:25:17.780 --> 00:25:19.010
They had destroyed them.

00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:20.720
- Now, we found those documents

00:25:20.720 --> 00:25:22.490
in the hands of another agency,

00:25:22.490 --> 00:25:24.470
so ultimately there was no harm.

00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:27.770
- Judge Tunheim said that, yes,
they got a lot of documents,

00:25:27.770 --> 00:25:30.050
but a lot of stuff was still missing.

00:25:30.050 --> 00:25:31.610
Like, there was one guy at the CIA

00:25:31.610 --> 00:25:33.440
who took control of the investigation

00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:35.570
a couple weeks after the assassination,

00:25:35.570 --> 00:25:39.080
and all of his records
are just unaccounted for.

00:25:39.080 --> 00:25:40.580
- Now, did he destroy them all?

00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:41.780
Maybe, I don't know.

00:25:41.780 --> 00:25:43.670
There's no real record of that,

00:25:43.670 --> 00:25:47.990
so you still have that
previously destroyed issue.

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:52.250
- In total, they finally
released 5 million documents

00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:53.360
by 2017,

00:25:53.360 --> 00:25:57.230
basically everything except
for a few thousand documents

00:25:57.230 --> 00:26:00.383
that the CIA still refuses to release.

00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:02.353
Why?

00:26:02.353 --> 00:26:03.186
Guys, come on.

00:26:03.186 --> 00:26:05.930
You can find this whole
trove of JFK documents

00:26:05.930 --> 00:26:07.700
on the National Archives' website.

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:09.020
We'll put a link in the description.

00:26:09.020 --> 00:26:11.450
Okay, but here's the
craziest part of all of this.

00:26:11.450 --> 00:26:14.150
Even after 5 million
documents were released

00:26:14.150 --> 00:26:15.110
to the American public,

00:26:15.110 --> 00:26:18.740
to a public that was like
hungry for like conspiracy,

00:26:18.740 --> 00:26:23.540
still, there is no solid-smoking
gun evidence in any of this

00:26:23.540 --> 00:26:25.850
that points to a conspiracy,

00:26:25.850 --> 00:26:28.760
that points to anyone other
than Lee Harvey Oswald

00:26:28.760 --> 00:26:30.950
as the person who
assassinated the President

00:26:30.950 --> 00:26:32.840
by himself, acting on his own.

00:26:32.840 --> 00:26:34.910
Now, the evidence may exist somewhere,

00:26:34.910 --> 00:26:36.170
but it's been destroyed or whatever.

00:26:36.170 --> 00:26:38.420
The point is, the government
could have released

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:41.030
these 5 million documents in the '60s.

00:26:41.030 --> 00:26:43.880
Like, they could have done this
back when people wanted it,

00:26:43.880 --> 00:26:44.810
back when they should have,

00:26:44.810 --> 00:26:46.760
and it wouldn't have
changed their official story

00:26:46.760 --> 00:26:49.310
and it would've satiated
an American public

00:26:49.310 --> 00:26:51.230
that was skeptical of their government.

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:53.900
At this point though,
I think it's too late.

00:26:53.900 --> 00:26:56.000
The feeling that the
government was hiding something

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:58.340
has now sunk deep into
the American psyche.

00:26:58.340 --> 00:26:59.247
We all kind of are like,

00:26:59.247 --> 00:27:01.640
"The JFK assassination, yes,
something was up there."

00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:02.690
I'm not really sure they're ever gonna

00:27:02.690 --> 00:27:04.370
regain our trust on this one

00:27:04.370 --> 00:27:06.770
because of how much hiding
of information there was

00:27:06.770 --> 00:27:08.300
throughout all of these decades.

00:27:08.300 --> 00:27:11.090
So on the internet, all around,

00:27:11.090 --> 00:27:12.830
from people who are
actually pretty credible,

00:27:12.830 --> 00:27:15.890
you have alternative
explanations that abound.

00:27:15.890 --> 00:27:17.750
Maybe it was LBJ who planned it

00:27:17.750 --> 00:27:18.980
so that he could be president.

00:27:18.980 --> 00:27:21.500
Or what I believe is perhaps
the most feasible theory,

00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:24.230
which is that some
rogue faction in the CIA

00:27:24.230 --> 00:27:25.460
wanted to take out JFK

00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:28.460
because JFK was against
what the CIA was up to.

00:27:28.460 --> 00:27:30.740
He was shutting down
their covert operations.

00:27:30.740 --> 00:27:33.230
And then there's, of course,
the idea that Cuba did it.

00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:37.100
I mean, that's what LBJ, the
president after JFK, thought.

00:27:37.100 --> 00:27:38.810
Like, he was like, "It was probably Cuba

00:27:38.810 --> 00:27:41.240
because we've been trying to
assassinate their leader."

00:27:41.240 --> 00:27:43.790
The point is that because
of the information vacuum

00:27:43.790 --> 00:27:47.300
left by the CIA and the
FBI holding back evidence

00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:48.440
from the American people,

00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:51.110
people started to look at
the evidence they did have

00:27:51.110 --> 00:27:55.340
and grasp at any evidence they
could find for conspiracy.

00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:57.650
They started connecting
the dots of the witnesses

00:27:57.650 --> 00:28:00.050
who met mysterious or suspicious deaths.

00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:03.530
Many theorists will fixate
on this mysterious man

00:28:03.530 --> 00:28:06.500
holding an umbrella in
this video on a sunny day,

00:28:06.500 --> 00:28:09.080
maybe giving the signal
to a second shooter?

00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:10.550
It's all very tantalizing,

00:28:10.550 --> 00:28:13.130
and some of it is actually very valid

00:28:13.130 --> 00:28:15.950
as like leads for further investigation.

00:28:15.950 --> 00:28:19.250
But despite a lot of really fishy stuff,

00:28:19.250 --> 00:28:21.860
I have not seen any solid evidence

00:28:21.860 --> 00:28:23.630
that proves an alternative story

00:28:23.630 --> 00:28:26.000
to the one that was told
to us back in the '60s

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:28.190
that Lee Harvey Oswald
was the guy who did it

00:28:28.190 --> 00:28:29.660
and he acted alone.

00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:30.860
I think it's very plausible

00:28:30.860 --> 00:28:32.900
that there could be some conspiracy.

00:28:32.900 --> 00:28:34.070
I think we will never know

00:28:34.070 --> 00:28:36.020
because we simply don't have the evidence.

00:28:36.020 --> 00:28:38.180
One thing I do know for certain though

00:28:38.180 --> 00:28:40.070
is that the moment this investigation

00:28:40.070 --> 00:28:42.740
turned into an effort
to stifle information

00:28:42.740 --> 00:28:45.320
and influence the facts
towards one conclusion,

00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:47.390
it laid the foundation for the public

00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:50.870
to turn this into a
cesspool of speculation.

00:28:50.870 --> 00:28:52.880
Again, I keep going back to that feeling

00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:54.740
of being lied to by your government.

00:28:54.740 --> 00:28:55.670
It's very potent.

00:28:55.670 --> 00:28:56.600
It sticks with you.

00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:58.070
It creates fertile ground

00:28:58.070 --> 00:29:01.040
for conspiracy theories
of all kinds to sprout.

00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:03.140
Because when you feel
like you're being lied to

00:29:03.140 --> 00:29:06.110
by your own democracy,
by your own leaders,

00:29:06.110 --> 00:29:08.510
no matter the reason or justification,

00:29:08.510 --> 00:29:10.760
it makes you feel like you're on your own,

00:29:10.760 --> 00:29:12.020
like no one's got your back,

00:29:12.020 --> 00:29:15.500
and that you are the one who
needs to find the real truth.

00:29:15.500 --> 00:29:17.930
And to me, it's that space

00:29:17.930 --> 00:29:20.600
that the most enduring conspiracy theories

00:29:20.600 --> 00:29:21.954
find their footing.

00:29:21.954 --> 00:29:25.550
(tense suspenseful music)

00:29:25.550 --> 00:29:28.500
- Have you ever committed any
act of violence in your life?

00:29:31.550 --> 00:29:32.488
- No.

00:29:32.488 --> 00:29:36.405
(tense suspenseful music ends)

